**[The Displacement Manifold — Cassian decides to talk]**

**GM** — *Cassian visibly weighing whether to speak*
> "She then, he then pauses at you, it looks as if he's deciding something, and says."

**GM (Lord Cassian Meliamne)** — *the lead*
> "Elara was investigating something. I don't know whether I should tell you it, but… Well, you did bring this…"
> "You did bring this artifact."
> "She was investigating the interplanar shipping device at the docks before she died."
> "The displacement manifold. It stopped working about 7 weeks ago. The commission was operating it as a commercial service. Goods arrive in Neverwinter by Sea, then the manifold distributes them to stores across the region."
> "Lionschild Koster was their primary client. All of their regional distribution ran through it. When it went dark, their store stopped receiving goods. Nobody official will say why. She believes the timing wasn't coincidental."
> "I told her that this wasn't her business, but she was very determined to go look into this."

**GM (Lord Cassian Meliamne)** — *the request*
> "since you did such a good turn and found this, and it would be… I would be much appreciative if you were to see if there was any connection between her investigations and her death."

**[The Gnome Technician]**

**GM (Lord Cassian Meliamne)** — *describing the missing gnome*
> "I pass on this. The device had a regular technician, a gnome. Lyra described him. She met him twice at the docks when she was tracking the shipping gap. Smaller, older, very precise, the kind of person who asks questions that go past the job."
> "She wrote that he seemed more interested in why the planar routing worked than whether it was functioning like he was mapping something. She found it unsettling at the time and didn't know why."
> "He hadn't seen… he hasn't been seen since, the magical manifold… the manifold stop. She didn't have a name for him, just the description and the questions he asked."

**Valphine** — *OOC recognition of the genre*
> "Planescape format."

**Valphine / GM** — *pressing for a name*
> "start, name?"
> "I didn't have it. This was one of these… this was one of Elara's things. She was the one who was interested in these things. I personally believe that when it comes to the Commission, one should"
> "Keep one's distance."

**[The Order of the Gauntlet Credential]**

**Vukradin** — *delivering the last message*
> "Well, thank you, Lord. Oh, I did have one other message to deliver."
> "The, the, the order, we brought this to you"
> "Under the auspices of the Order of the Gauntlet."

**GM (Lord Cassian Meliamne)** — *reaction*
> "He smiles, like, he goes, yes, yes, the order of the gauntlet. And he pauses and goes."
> "They are truly one of the few heroes of the realms."
> "Like, it turns out, like, he sees them as the good guys."

**GM** — *confirming Cassian's sincerity*
> "Yeah, no, he's not a… he's not giving you the vibe of being…"

**Vukradin**
> "That's good."
